OK, if you are reading this you are probably thinking whether playing this game or not. Let me try to write a helpful review with no spoilers:
good:
-story: although many say that it is going too far at the end;
- characters: 3 main characters, a murderer and two detectives. Very memorable, stereotyped in a good way;
- game concept/mechanics: the story is divided to chapters. Each chapter is a few minutes long and you play as one of the main character (sometimes with both detectives). You micromanage single actions to progress. There are about 5 major action to complete and few minor, which may make your job easier/harder through particular chapter;
- sound and music: really good voice acting too;
- atmosphere: mystery, crime solving, some easy puzzles, some minor elements of comedy and horror;
neutral:
- graphics: a little old, but still let the graphics DO NOT DISCOURAGE you to play this game (sorry for caps), ... and Carla's lips are always shining so hot that i want to kiss my monitor;
- controls: outdated, still i finished the game with mouse and keyboard and had absolutely no problems. DO NOT SKIP this game because of controls (oops, sorry for my caps again);
bad:
- QTE: alot of them. May become annoying and boring soon. Implemented in such a silly way that i was laughing sometimes how basic they are, also very easy to complete;
PS: oh yes, and the opening scene .. I was replaying it and watching on web a few times ... amazing!

